<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hilla</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as al-Hilla</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hilla, or al-Hilla, is a city in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> on a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a>, near the ruins of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a>. It was founded around 1101 by the Mazyadid emir <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sadaqa-ibn-mansur">Sadaqa ibn Mansur</a> as the capital of his Arab principality and soon became a leading centre of Shia scholarship, home to theologians such as al-Allama al-Hilli. It is the capital of Babil <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/governorate">Governorate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hilla.jpg" alt="Hilla" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: إعلام مستشفى النور للأطفال · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Al-Noor_Hospital_for_Pediatrics.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
